Windows & Active Directory Fundamentals
Notes and takeaways from today's study session on TryHackMe covering Windows OS internals and account structures.
📌 Core Architecture
•	System32 Directory: Contains the core files for the Windows operating system.
•	System Criticality: Deleting or altering files within System32 can render the Windows OS completely inoperable.
⚙️ Environment Variables
•	Definition: Environment variables store crucial information about the operating system environment.
•	System Directory: The standard system environment variable for the primary Windows directory is %windir%.
👥 User Account Structures
Local Windows systems categorize user accounts into specific types:
•	Administrator: Full system access and control.
•	Standard User: Restricted access for daily tasks.
•	Guest: The built-in account used for temporary access 
